  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Where this fits",
      "items": [
        "This is the Native fused MoE box in the decoder-layer overview. It applies to B4 at T17-32 and MAIN above T32.",
        "Tiny, Tiny2 and MID use their separate warp-specialized paths. The four-warpgroup topology does not describe T1 or T8."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Two expert phases in the same launch",
      "items": [
        "Phase A computes gate and up projections, then SiLU(gate) multiplied by up. It publishes intermediate BF16 rows in global memory.",
        "Phase B waits for its required rows, loads them through the activation producer and ring, and computes the down projection.",
        "Full expert RMS and routing-weight combination produce the local expert sum. Readiness is per dependency; CTAs can enter Phase B at different times."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Scheduling and lifetime",
      "items": [
        "Cost-weighted stream-K can split an output unit across CTAs. Global partials and a designated finisher resolve those splits.",
        "Weight codes and scales move into registers before the weight slot is released. Activation-slot reuse follows WGMMA retirement and the retained fence.",
        "Slot counts and thread counts describe resources. No internal microsecond attribution is asserted."
      ]
    }
  ]
